      "problem": "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-{x}_{2}{y}_{3}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-{x}_{2}{y}_{3}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2-3+0-4 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
